<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Extra WiX source for the `server` component MSI (TASK-147/249), linked in
  via -D CPACK_WIX_EXTRA_SOURCES alongside CPack's auto-generated fragments
  (same mechanism client-extra.wxs already uses for the client MSI).

  TASK-249: the server MSI as originally shipped never created
  server.conf at all. server-patch.xml only adds ServiceInstall/
  ServiceControl/FirewallException, and CMakeLists.txt's own
  server.conf.example install() rule is Linux-only (destined for
  share/vapourwault, consumed by the DEB/RPM postinst scripts). Contrast
  with the manual Install-VaporWault.ps1 path, which explicitly copies
  server.conf.example to %ProgramData%\VaporWault\server.conf if absent.

  FIRST ATTEMPT (abandoned): a Component/@NeverOverwrite="yes" File
  installed directly to CommonAppDataFolder\VaporWault\server.conf. Built
  and installed correctly in isolation (fresh install created the file;
  a standalone reinstall of the same version left an edited copy alone),
  but real upgrade testing (TASK-249/152: install 1.0.0, edit config,
  install 1.0.1 with CPack's default `MajorUpgrade
  Schedule="afterInstallInitialize"`) found it does NOT survive a real
  major upgrade: the file was gone afterward, not just left alone. Log
  analysis: the new version's own action-table computation resolves this
  shared-GUID component to Action=Null (it sees the file already present,
  owned by the related old product about to be removed, and decides
  nothing needs installing) while the OLD version's nested
  RemoveExistingProducts removal computes Action=Absent for the very same
  component and deletes the file; neither side ends up owning/keeping
  it. NeverOverwrite's documented semantics ("only for components
  registered by the Registry table"... "does register itself as a client
  of the component") are for components shared between *unrelated*
  products, not a single product's own file surviving its own version
  upgrades; it does not compose safely with CPack's early-scheduled
  RemoveExistingProducts here. Not chasing MajorUpgrade's Schedule
  attribute as an alternative fix: CPackWiXFragment can only add children
  to an element it matches by Id, and <MajorUpgrade> has no Id to match
  in the first place.

  SECOND ATTEMPT (also abandoned): an IMMEDIATE CustomAction using a
  [#FileId] token to copy server.conf.example (installed as an ordinary,
  always-overwritten reference file) to server.conf if absent. No
  deferred/CustomActionData two-step seemed necessary since this server
  install is fully elevated throughout (no impersonation/session
  boundary to work around, unlike the client's per-user Scheduled Task),
  and immediate actions have full Property/File-table access. This also
  failed a real test: the action ran before InstallFiles' own actual file
  copy happened even though scheduled After="InstallFiles" (InstallFiles
  is itself a deferred standard action, so "After" only orders entries in
  the sequence table, not when each one's real file-system work
  executes). The token resolved to a path, but nothing existed there
  yet, so the copy failed every time.

  FIX ACTUALLY USED: the CustomAction below is Execute="deferred" with
  Directory="CM_DP_server.bin" (the real bin folder) as its working
  directory, referencing server.conf.example by plain relative filename
  once it's actually been copied there. A Directory attribute resolves
  correctly for a deferred action even though a [Property]/
  [CustomActionData] token inside ExeCommand does not (same fix TASK-247
  verified for the client MSI). This sidesteps both MSI's component
  reference-counting (the first attempt's problem) and the immediate/
  deferred timing gap (the second attempt's problem), runs
  deterministically on every install/upgrade/repair, and is what actually
  survived a real upgrade test with an edited config in place.
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/wi">

  <Fragment>
    <DirectoryRef Id="CM_DP_server.bin">
      <!-- Fixed GUID: must never change once shipped. (Deliberately a
           fresh one, not reused from the abandoned NeverOverwrite
           attempt above: that was a different directory, different
           File, different semantics; reusing its GUID for an unrelated
           component would only confuse anyone later tracing this GUID's
           history.) -->
      <Component Id="VWServerConfigExampleComponent" Guid="DE254733-4CF5-4003-A3A3-1B9BB7D5F2E7">
        <File Id="VWServerConfigExampleFile"
              Source="$(var.VW_WIX_DIR)\..\server.conf.example"
              Name="server.conf.example"
              KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
    </DirectoryRef>

    <!-- Execute="deferred", not immediate, and Directory="CM_DP_server.bin"
         with a plain relative source filename instead of a [#FileId]
         token: found for real that an IMMEDIATE custom action scheduled
         After="InstallFiles" still runs before InstallFiles' own actual
         file copy happens (InstallFiles is itself a deferred standard
         action; "After" only orders entries in the sequence table, not
         when each one's real file-system work executes). The
         [#VWServerConfigExampleFile] token resolved to a path, but
         nothing existed there yet, so the copy failed. A Directory
         attribute, unlike a [Property]/[CustomActionData] token inside
         ExeCommand, does resolve correctly for a deferred action (same
         fix TASK-247 already verified for the client MSI), so this next
         attempt sidesteps the token/path entirely by making the working
         directory the real bin folder and referencing the file by plain
         name once it's actually there. -->
    <CustomAction Id="TemplateServerConfig"
        Directory="CM_DP_server.bin"
        Execute="deferred"
        Return="ignore"
        ExeCommand="powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command &quot;New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path 'C:\ProgramData\VaporWault' | Out-Null; if (-not (Test-Path 'C:\ProgramData\VaporWault\server.conf')) { Copy-Item 'server.conf.example' 'C:\ProgramData\VaporWault\server.conf' }&quot;" />

    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <Custom Action="TemplateServerConfig" After="InstallFiles">NOT REMOVE</Custom>
    </InstallExecuteSequence>
  </Fragment>

</Wix>
